{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1388900-question","id":1388900,"title":"Question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-16T05:58:23-07:00","id":1388900,"title":"Question","content":"Is there any OFFICIAL 2nd edition God with a wolf as 'rotemic' animal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T06:12:10-07:00","id":1388906,"title":"","content":"What is: rotemic animal? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T06:33:44-07:00","id":1388910,"title":"","content":"Assuming you mean the Purview Specialization mechanic... currently no, though the Demigod book is set to contain the Tengri, the Mongolian Gods, who do have wolf-related deities.<br /> <br /> However, in case you're asking for your character a reminder that you can specialize the Beasts Purview (or choose not to specialize at all) as you wish... you are not limited by your Patron, so a Scion of Ganesha need not take Beasts (Elephant)... you can take Beasts (Zebra) or choose to just take Beasts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T06:35:28-07:00","id":1388912,"title":"","content":"It really depends on what you expect a totemic animal to be.<br /> There is the Creature birthright where a scion could take a wolf.<br /> The Guide Birtheight would also allow a scion taking the Wolf Dodaem as a Guide.<br /> <br /> The Ojibwe, the people of the Manitou pantheon found in the core book, have a family clan of wolf (Ma'iigan in this case i think).<br /> And i think the Haudonesaunee, the people of the Orenda, also found in the core book also have a family clan of wolf.<br /> All that said family clan dont exactly work the way you might be expecting so i would advise doing a bit of research on the subject before going further (i know i will).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T10:06:38-07:00","id":1388980,"title":"","content":"Cheeby-aub-oozzoo in the Manitou Pantheon has Beast (Wolf). He\u2019s their god of the dead, by virtue of having died.<br /> <br /> As Samudra said though, if you\u2019re just asking for your own character, if you inherit Beast from your parent/patron, you are not restricted on if or how you specialize it. You want a Scion with Beast (Wolf) innate as Chosen of Artemis, or Daughter of Sobek, or Son of Inari - you are absolutely free to do that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 05-16-2020, 01:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}